  "comment": "The fixed classes of the distinctive-token guard (docs/design/core.md §4.5), written as the institution normalizer leaves them ('tech' is already 'technology'). Cities, regions, countries and campuses are derived by the build: cities from IPEDS CITY and every ROR candidate's location (not only the bundled records), regions from regions.json, countries from CLDR and countries.aliases.json, campuses from IPEDS campus suffixes. The discipline class is derived from the words of CIP 2020's family and series titles (2 and 4 digits, the non-credit families 32-37 left out), minus stopwords, the words of the other fixed classes and disciplineIgnore (words that only say what kind of program a title is, not what it is about); 'discipline' adds words CIP's titles lack. campusPhrases adds multi-word campus names; cities adds the English exonyms and former names job sites and resumes still use (Bombay for Mumbai, Peking for Beijing) and campus towns no ROR location holds (Mississauga); campusIgnore lists the words of IPEDS campus suffixes that say nothing about a campus ('Adult Degree Programs', 'Main Campus').",
